# Cloudflare's headers file. `public/` is copied verbatim into `out/`, so this
# lands at the root of the deployed site, which is where Cloudflare reads it.
#
# Only one rule here earns its place, and it is about `curl … | sh`.
#
# **`text/plain`, deliberately.** `.sh` would otherwise be served as a type the
# browser downloads, and the front page links to this file as *the script* — an
# installer nobody can read before running is an installer nobody should run.
# `curl` does not care either way, so plain text costs the pipe nothing and buys
# a reader everything. `nosniff` then stops a browser second-guessing it.
#
# **Five minutes, not a year.** This file is fetched once per machine and never
# again — the script and `lingtai upgrade` both go straight to GitHub Releases
# after that — so there is nothing to gain from a long cache, and a bug fixed in
# the installer wants to reach the next person rather than the next year's.
/install.sh
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
